# A recorded `act --json` stream, one JSON object per line.
#
# Recorded from a real one-step workflow under `act`, then reduced to the
# events the parser reads. Fields no parser touches and that vary per machine
# or per run — `time`, `msg`, `jobID`, `jobPath` and the container paths inside
# `msg` — are dropped, so the file is deterministic and diffs cleanly.
#
# Lines starting with `#` are not part of the format; the test strips them.
#
# the one shape where `act` emits the same output name twice.
#
# A name reaches this stream more than once only when a step writes it through
# the *legacy* `::set-output::` command: `act` walks the log lines as they
# arrive and emits one event per command, so a `$GITHUB_OUTPUT` write followed
# by a legacy one (and then another file write) yields two events. Ordinary
# `$GITHUB_OUTPUT` writes are folded by the runner and emit a single event
# carrying the final value — see
# `docs/adr-012-actions-runner-integration-harness.md`.
#
# The recorded workflow wrote `value=from-file`, then
# `::set-output name=value::from-legacy-command`, then `value=from-file-again`,
# and read back `from-file-again`. So the live value is the *last* event's, and
# a parser that took the first match would report a value the run had already
# replaced.
#
{"step": "Set up job", "stepResult": "success"}
{"arg": "from-legacy-command", "command": "set-output", "name": "value", "step": "Write one output three ways"}
{"arg": "from-file-again", "command": "set-output", "name": "value", "step": "Write one output three ways"}
{"step": "Write one output three ways", "stepResult": "success"}
{"step": "Read it back", "stepResult": "success"}
{"step": "Complete job", "stepResult": "success"}
